From: William Horvath <william@horvath.blog>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Respect cursor visibility for tablet tools in ShowCursor

Wayland_ShowCursor set mouse->cur_cursor on tablet tools regardless of the
cursor passed in, so SDL_HideCursor() never hid the cursor of a tool that
was already in proximity; only the next proximity-in applied it.
---
--- a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandmouse.c
+++ b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandmouse.c
@@ -1133,16 +1133,12 @@
 
         SDL_WaylandPenTool *tool;
         wl_list_for_each(tool, &seat->tablet.tool_list, link) {
-            obj.wl_tool = tool->wltool;
-            obj.is_pointer = false;
-
-            /* The current cursor is explicitly set on tablet tools, as there may be no pointer device, or
-             * the pointer may not have focus, which would instead cause the default cursor to be set.
+            /* The cursor is derived from the mouse state for tablet tools, as there may be no pointer device, or
+             * the pointer may not have focus, which would instead cause the default cursor to be set (and the
+             * cursor passed in here would not reflect a hidden cursor).
              */
-            if (tool->focus && (!mouse->focus || mouse->focus->internal == tool->focus)) {
-                Wayland_CursorStateSetCursor(&tool->cursor_state, &obj, tool->focus, tool->proximity_serial, mouse->cur_cursor);
-            } else if (!tool->focus) {
-                Wayland_CursorStateResetCursor(&tool->cursor_state);
+            if (!tool->focus || !mouse->focus || mouse->focus->internal == tool->focus) {
+                Wayland_TabletToolUpdateCursor(tool);
             }
         }
     }
